applied to the pinned commit by mineai/fetch-and-patch.sh (or scripts/mineai-fetch.mjs); git apply skips these lines.
0010: build_structure never stops the runtime's event loop, and builds a shelter around the bot. A 1x1 shelter around
the bot (four walls two high and a roof, the bot's own cells asked to be air) in a 1x2 pocket in stone: every
placement read as sealing the bot in, so the build asked for a route out of the structure; the route completed where
the bot stood (its goal already met) and the loop asked again, forever, with nothing real to await, until the
supervisor's watchdog ended the runtime (RUNTIME_UNRESPONSIVE; 4 of 4 bench tries and once through the gateway,
2026-10-08); on open ground the same shelter stopped at 9 of 10 ("could not step out of the structure"). Now no
placement is held back as enclosing when the bot is meant to be inside (the request asks for the cell its feet stand
in to be air) or the world already walls it in; steps out of the structure in a row that change nothing stop the
build after 3 with the reason; and every pass of the loop yields to the event loop. With tests (build-process; the
two loop cases hung before the patch).

